  "details": "since the 2018 update, a syncvideostream component in a world does not auto-start anymore. \nthis (doesn't) happen (anymore) to existing world uploaded with older unity (2017.4.19) which were functionnal before the update, and also happen with the new 2018.4.20 version. \nthis has been tried with the latest SDK, latest Unity (fresh project form this morning) using the latest Jetdog Prefab and also by creating the component manually\n\nthe only workaround at the moment is to add a trigger and use the SendRPC.Play or SendRPC.Next (or use the ui included in jetdog's prefab)\n\nsince this was functionnal and a desired effect for most club worlds, it would be nice to either see this fixed, or to get documentation on how to properly setup RPCs for multiple use case (movies, livestreams, etc)",
